1
00:00:01,334 --> 00:00:02,376
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:02,502 --> 00:00:03,794
"I can't do this anymore."

3
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:06,923
You can't keep pulling me
from the path of oncoming trains.

4
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:09,091
There's new trains coming
every day.

5
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:10,718
You have information
about the case?

6
00:00:10,843 --> 00:00:12,970
My brother does. Gabriel.
He's a psychic.

7
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:14,597
There's a thing inside you.

8
00:00:15,306 --> 00:00:17,099
"Your cure will come
with the number three."

9
00:00:18,559 --> 00:00:19,852
I didn't know where you were.

10
00:00:19,977 --> 00:00:22,063
- You knew I'd be back.
- No, I didn't.

11
00:00:22,271 --> 00:00:23,481
There's a serial killer

12
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:25,900
"with an evil heart
and an appetite to kill."

13
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:28,569
I saw that the killer
is going to kill again. Tonight.

14
00:00:30,279 --> 00:00:32,823
"Why would the killer care
if Gabriel was a real psychic?"

15
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:35,993
"He wants one for some reason
and Gabriel didn't pass the test."

16
00:00:38,204 --> 00:00:40,831
- "Could you just take a look?"
- "He was sitting in the car, right?"

17
00:00:40,998 --> 00:00:42,833
The whole time I was putting out
the trash

18
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,378
he just sat there, staring at me.

19
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:47,672
They still haven't caught that guy
who killed those people.

20
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,507
It could be him. You don't know.

21
00:00:50,341 --> 00:00:53,928
Serial killers don't sit in cars.
They lurk in the shadows.

22
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:56,430
Be right back.

23
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:35,636
Hey.

24
00:01:45,605 --> 00:01:46,647
Stupid drunk.

25
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:52,486
Oh!

26
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:56,449
Susan!

27
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:03,873
Soos?

28
00:02:17,803 --> 00:02:18,846
Soos?

29
00:02:24,101 --> 00:02:25,144
"What is this?"

30
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,646
Did you buy me another horse?

31
00:02:28,105 --> 00:02:29,607
- Just a little further.
- Okay.

32
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,443
Is this a trick?

33
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:36,072
- Breathe that air in.
- Okay, I'm breathing in that air.

34
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,948
And... voilà.

35
00:02:41,577 --> 00:02:43,621
Jane... what is this?

36
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:47,500
It's a little shack that I'm gonna renovate
make some additions.

37
00:02:47,875 --> 00:02:49,377
We both knew things had to change.

38
00:02:49,502 --> 00:02:53,547
I-I couldn't make you quit,
and I need something to do.

39
00:02:53,964 --> 00:02:55,966
- So you're gonna build us a house.
- That's right.

40
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:57,968
And when I'm done, if nothing else

41
00:02:58,344 --> 00:02:59,512
we have a place to live.

42
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:01,389
It's a start.

43
00:03:01,597 --> 00:03:03,683
So you're gonna work here, not...
not at the FBI.

44
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,643
- You're quitting.
- Maybe. I-I don't know.

45
00:03:05,768 --> 00:03:06,852
I haven't decided yet.

46
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:11,232
What?

47
00:03:13,150 --> 00:03:15,945
I'm glad you got it. I am.
But...

48
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:17,822
I have needs, too.

49
00:03:19,198 --> 00:03:20,241
Like what?

50
00:03:21,784 --> 00:03:23,619
I need to know
that you're not gonna run away again.

51
00:03:23,744 --> 00:03:24,787
I won't.

52
00:03:24,912 --> 00:03:27,039
I need to know
that you're committed to this, to us.

53
00:03:27,373 --> 00:03:29,458
I-I am. That's why I wanna do this.

54
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:33,546
Okay.

55
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:36,340
Then are you gonna take off
your wedding ring?

56
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:40,803
It just, it seems like
you don't wanna let go of it.

57
00:03:41,178 --> 00:03:44,890
- No, it's not that.
- I-I understand why it's difficult for you.

58
00:03:45,015 --> 00:03:47,518
- It-it's just that I'm used to it.
- I know. It...

59
00:03:54,483 --> 00:03:55,526
What's up, boss?

60
00:03:55,651 --> 00:03:57,570
"Sorry, Lisbon.
I know you're on your way home."

61
00:03:57,695 --> 00:03:58,779
"But I need you to turn around."

62
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,448
We have another one.

63
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:18,380
The victim's name is Susan Herman.

64
00:04:18,964 --> 00:04:21,425
Her husband reported her
missing last night.

65
00:04:22,050 --> 00:04:24,094
Apparently, the killer snatched
her off her porch.

66
00:04:24,219 --> 00:04:26,430
- That's a change.
- The pattern's the same otherwise...

67
00:04:26,555 --> 00:04:28,557
Shot in the chest,
one fingernail ripped off.

68
00:04:28,682 --> 00:04:29,933
He didn't bother hiding the body.

69
00:04:30,267 --> 00:04:31,310
Could mean he's getting bolder.

70
00:04:31,602 --> 00:04:32,728
Or more playful.

71
00:04:33,187 --> 00:04:34,480
- Playful?
- Well, sure.

72
00:04:34,938 --> 00:04:37,232
{\an8}He knows we're on to him.
That's why he left her out for us to find.

73
00:04:37,357 --> 00:04:39,318
{\an8}- He's also done something else.
- What?

74
00:04:40,152 --> 00:04:41,195
I'm not sure.

75
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:42,863
Uh, excuse me.

76
00:04:43,155 --> 00:04:45,949
{\an8}That mark on her left arm...
is that a puncture wound?

77
00:04:47,534 --> 00:04:48,577
Looks like it.

78
00:04:48,702 --> 00:04:50,370
- Is that from a needle?
- Uh, little bigger.

79
00:04:50,704 --> 00:04:52,039
Could be from an IV line.

80
00:04:52,414 --> 00:04:55,292
{\an8}Why would he put an IV In her?
Uh, he's not poisoning them.

81
00:04:55,417 --> 00:04:58,462
{\an8}I don't think he was putting anything in.
More likely, he was taking something out.

82
00:04:58,670 --> 00:05:00,422
{\an8}Could be right. Position the body correctly

83
00:05:00,547 --> 00:05:02,299
{\an8}you can take out a cup or more
of blood with an IV.

84
00:05:02,716 --> 00:05:06,345
{\an8}So he kills them, rips out a fingernail
and takes a cup of blood.

85
00:05:09,306 --> 00:05:11,225
{\an8}And we're making every possible effort.

86
00:05:12,434 --> 00:05:14,520
{\an8}Thanks. All right, thanks for calling.

87
00:05:16,855 --> 00:05:19,483
Everyone and his sister wants to know
when we're making an arrest.

88
00:05:20,442 --> 00:05:22,653
{\an8}Right. This is Rick Tork
from the Santa Fe office.

89
00:05:22,778 --> 00:05:24,154
{\an8}He's gonna help out
while we're short-handed.

90
00:05:24,279 --> 00:05:25,322
{\an8}Hey.

91
00:05:25,447 --> 00:05:27,074
{\an8}Dennis Abbott. Thanks for coming.

92
00:05:27,366 --> 00:05:29,701
{\an8}- So, how long were you in Santa Fe?
- Uh, just a year.

93
00:05:29,910 --> 00:05:32,162
{\an8}I started out CBI, made the jump
to the federal side

94
00:05:32,287 --> 00:05:34,790
{\an8}- about the same time as Cho.
- And he's worked with Jane before.

95
00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:37,167
- Enough to know the score.
- And what's that?

96
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,211
He'll never tell you what he's up to.

97
00:05:39,503 --> 00:05:41,129
Whatever he does,
you'll look like an idiot.

98
00:05:41,839 --> 00:05:43,006
And always keep your hand
on your wallet.

99
00:05:43,465 --> 00:05:44,925
{\an8}Well, you do know the man.

100
00:05:46,552 --> 00:05:49,346
{\an8}I appreciate you coming tonight.
This case is blowing up.

101
00:05:49,471 --> 00:05:51,682
{\an8}- I hear you have 10 bodies.
- Yeah, five were found buried

102
00:05:51,807 --> 00:05:53,392
{\an8}killed between two and nine months ago.

103
00:05:53,809 --> 00:05:55,185
{\an8}Two were killed in their car last week

104
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:57,396
{\an8}Gabriel Osborne and his sister
a few days after that

105
00:05:57,563 --> 00:06:00,566
{\an8}- and the woman today.
- Wow. Any, uh, physical evidence?

106
00:06:01,066 --> 00:06:02,359
{\an8}Just the bullets...
they match

107
00:06:02,484 --> 00:06:03,902
but we haven't been able
to trace 'em to a gun.

108
00:06:04,027 --> 00:06:06,113
Tork, I heard you were here.
It's good to see you.

109
00:06:06,363 --> 00:06:08,115
- You, too.
- Anything from the profilers?

110
00:06:08,323 --> 00:06:10,993
{\an8}Uh, they can't find any patterns
in the killings.

111
00:06:11,326 --> 00:06:13,287
{\an8}Uh, the first two victims were homeless men

112
00:06:13,412 --> 00:06:14,788
the third was a prostitute.

113
00:06:14,997 --> 00:06:17,416
{\an8}The next ones
were foreign-exchange students

114
00:06:17,541 --> 00:06:19,418
{\an8}and then the couple in the car.

115
00:06:19,585 --> 00:06:22,254
{\an8}There's no consistency
in age, race, or gender.

116
00:06:22,379 --> 00:06:25,799
{\an8}I don't think this is about who he killed
so much as what he killed for.

117
00:06:25,924 --> 00:06:27,467
Hey, Tork. Long time, no see.

118
00:06:27,593 --> 00:06:28,844
Do you mean the blood
and the fingernails?

119
00:06:28,969 --> 00:06:31,805
{\an8}Well, fingernails not so much.
I think they're just a gruesome trophy.

120
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:33,891
{\an8}But the blood he had to work for.

121
00:06:34,016 --> 00:06:35,559
{\an8}He must need it for something.

122
00:06:35,684 --> 00:06:37,686
Did any of the other victims
have puncture wounds?

123
00:06:37,811 --> 00:06:40,856
Uh, the recent ones, yes.
The buried victims, we couldn't tell.

124
00:06:40,981 --> 00:06:42,316
The bodies had decomposed.

125
00:06:42,441 --> 00:06:45,360
I think we can assume he's been taking
blood samples for some time.

126
00:06:45,652 --> 00:06:48,655
- The question is why.
- There are some theories online.

127
00:06:48,947 --> 00:06:52,117
The most popular theory
is that he's a vampire of some sort.

128
00:06:52,242 --> 00:06:54,536
- Not sure if that's helpful.
- Well, maybe it is.

129
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:57,122
- Really?
- Well, he is stealing blood from a corpse.

130
00:06:57,247 --> 00:06:58,874
He's gotta be doing something weird
with it.

131
00:06:58,999 --> 00:07:00,375
So, he could be interested in the occult.

132
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,920
He believes in psychics.
That's why he went after Gabriel.

133
00:07:03,378 --> 00:07:04,922
Talk to Austin PD,
see if they have anything

134
00:07:05,047 --> 00:07:06,882
on local cults and nontraditional religions.

135
00:07:07,341 --> 00:07:09,843
Ask Homeland Security if they have
anything useful in their databases.

136
00:07:10,010 --> 00:07:12,429
Well, if he's interested in psychics
Jane should talk to him.

137
00:07:13,847 --> 00:07:16,683
Uh... Not a psychic, dude.

138
00:07:16,808 --> 00:07:17,893
No, but you can fake it, right?

139
00:07:18,936 --> 00:07:20,228
We could feed you to the media

140
00:07:20,437 --> 00:07:22,481
say that you can communicate
with the afterlife

141
00:07:22,606 --> 00:07:24,483
using your spiritual whatever.

142
00:07:24,608 --> 00:07:26,610
If he's really into that,
we can get him to show himself.

143
00:07:27,069 --> 00:07:30,489
The Son of Sam killer sent letters to two
of the writers who wrote about him.

144
00:07:30,781 --> 00:07:32,199
Hey, this kinda thing could really work.

145
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,620
Did I... say something wrong?

146
00:07:36,870 --> 00:07:38,246
Yeah, the last time Jane tried
something like that

147
00:07:38,372 --> 00:07:39,414
it didn't go well.

148
00:07:40,290 --> 00:07:42,542
- Oh, the wife and kid.
- Yeah, the wife and kid.

149
00:07:46,088 --> 00:07:50,801
Hey, uh, I meant to tell you
we got Gabriel's autopsy reports back.

150
00:07:51,843 --> 00:07:55,722
He had oligodendrogliomas...
they're tiny, little tumors in the brain.

151
00:07:55,847 --> 00:07:57,808
According to the coroner,
they can cause seizures

152
00:07:57,933 --> 00:08:00,227
blackouts, or delusional episodes.

153
00:08:00,352 --> 00:08:03,230
Poor kid. No wonder he thought
he was psychic.

154
00:08:03,689 --> 00:08:05,649
There's no such thing as psychics.

155
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:07,943
No.

156
00:08:09,820 --> 00:08:12,364
I shouldn't have said anything
about the ring. I'm sorry.

157
00:08:12,531 --> 00:08:14,199
- Teresa, please.
- Really, look...

158
00:08:14,324 --> 00:08:15,742
you do what you need to.

159
00:08:16,034 --> 00:08:17,577
I'm okay, I swear.

160
00:08:20,455 --> 00:08:23,041
We just got a call from Austin PD.
They think they have the serial killer.

161
00:08:23,166 --> 00:08:25,168
- Did they arrest him?
- The call said somebody shot him.

162
00:08:34,636 --> 00:08:36,680
- This does not seem right.
- It's a false alarm.

163
00:08:37,014 --> 00:08:40,058
A case of mistaken identity.
This is Sharon Nieto, Austin Homicide.

164
00:08:40,559 --> 00:08:42,144
The dead man is Le Kong Vinh.

165
00:08:42,394 --> 00:08:44,938
According to the neighbors
he goes around collecting recyclables.

166
00:08:45,063 --> 00:08:46,189
The homeowner was asleep

167
00:08:46,314 --> 00:08:48,066
when he heard banging
on the side of the house.

168
00:08:48,233 --> 00:08:49,985
It was Mr. Vinh going through
his garbage

169
00:08:50,277 --> 00:08:51,319
but he didn't know that.

170
00:08:51,445 --> 00:08:54,448
He thought somebody was trying
to break in so he grabs his trusty .38.

171
00:08:54,573 --> 00:08:56,074
Homeowner issued a challenge
through the door.

172
00:08:56,199 --> 00:08:58,326
- Just heard more banging.
- And Vinh didn't speak English.

173
00:08:58,493 --> 00:08:59,536
That's right.

174
00:08:59,703 --> 00:09:01,788
So he fires through the door, calls us

175
00:09:01,913 --> 00:09:03,373
says he shot a serial killer.

176
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,542
- Is that the victim's wife?
- Yeah.

177
00:09:06,001 --> 00:09:07,836
I guess they were collecting
the bottles together.

178
00:09:10,172 --> 00:09:12,883
Are you guys gonna catch
this whack job anytime soon?

179
00:09:13,008 --> 00:09:15,385
People are freaked out.
We're getting calls all day.

180
00:09:15,552 --> 00:09:17,137
Is your department logging
all the calls?

181
00:09:17,429 --> 00:09:18,555
- Sure.
- Then we need that log.

182
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,976
Ah, it's a tough situation.

183
00:09:23,143 --> 00:09:26,063
The city is in a full-on panic,
and we have no solid leads.

184
00:09:27,230 --> 00:09:28,648
Okay, well, uh...

185
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:32,402
- Do we try Tork's idea?
- What? No.

186
00:09:32,819 --> 00:09:34,404
I don't think that we can rule
anything out.

187
00:09:34,613 --> 00:09:35,655
Boss.

188
00:09:36,281 --> 00:09:38,283
The guy is not hiding bodies anymore.

189
00:09:38,408 --> 00:09:41,620
You know, maybe he's starting to...
to like the attention.

190
00:09:41,745 --> 00:09:44,331
Do you want him to do to Jane
what he did to Gabriel?

191
00:09:44,581 --> 00:09:45,916
Now, you know
we won't let that happen.

192
00:09:46,041 --> 00:09:47,626
- You can't promise that!
- Y-you know what?

193
00:09:47,751 --> 00:09:50,879
I appreciate your spirited defense but it...
it's not necessary.

194
00:09:51,922 --> 00:09:52,964
I'll do it.

195
00:09:54,508 --> 00:09:55,550
Okay.

196
00:09:59,954 --> 00:10:01,623
{\an8}"According to state forestry officials"

197
00:10:01,748 --> 00:10:02,790
{\an8}"once the bear was tranquilized"

198
00:10:02,916 --> 00:10:04,792
"he was relocated to a wilderness area."

199
00:10:05,585 --> 00:10:07,462
"And now an update
from our AccuWeather desk."

200
00:10:07,629 --> 00:10:11,049
I'm gonna say this one last time.
You don't have to do this.

201
00:10:11,216 --> 00:10:12,258
I know that.

202
00:10:12,675 --> 00:10:15,595
Coming up, a psychic
who's working with the FBI.

203
00:10:15,762 --> 00:10:17,680
You're watching Austin Today.
Stay with us.

204
00:10:18,139 --> 00:10:19,599
We're out. Back in 60.

205
00:10:28,608 --> 00:10:29,651
Oh, you've done this before?

206
00:10:31,069 --> 00:10:32,111
Yep.

207
00:10:32,904 --> 00:10:34,822
All right, I'm gonna throw you
a couple easy questions

208
00:10:34,948 --> 00:10:36,282
we'll have some fun,
just keep the ball in the air.

209
00:10:36,491 --> 00:10:37,700
- Sure.
- "Back in 10."

210
00:10:39,285 --> 00:10:42,038
5, 4, 3...

211
00:10:43,915 --> 00:10:46,251
{\an8}"Welcome back to Austin Today.
I'm Dan Glover."

212
00:10:46,376 --> 00:10:49,587
{\an8}"And with me is Patrick Jane
a psychic who works with the FBI."

213
00:10:51,798 --> 00:10:54,217
I'd like to talk about how you're helping
to hunt

214
00:10:54,342 --> 00:10:55,885
for the man
who's believed to have murdered

215
00:10:56,010 --> 00:10:59,013
a number of our local citizens
but first I have to ask...

216
00:10:59,514 --> 00:11:01,474
What is a psychic?
What is it you do?

217
00:11:06,271 --> 00:11:07,313
Patrick?

218
00:11:07,605 --> 00:11:10,191
- Patrick?
- Yeah, Dan, sorry, I was distracted.

219
00:11:10,316 --> 00:11:11,943
Um, there's something on your mind.

220
00:11:12,068 --> 00:11:15,405
Your wife, uh... just had a baby...
a girl, I believe.

221
00:11:16,823 --> 00:11:18,241
- Who told you that?
- You did.

222
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:23,204
Uh, her, her name begins
with a vowel, A, E, A...

223
00:11:23,329 --> 00:11:26,457
Alexa, uh...
Alexa, right?

224
00:11:26,583 --> 00:11:28,126
That's... right.

225
00:11:29,502 --> 00:11:31,879
- So that's how you do it, huh?
- That's how I do it, Dan.

226
00:11:32,255 --> 00:11:33,673
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

227
00:11:34,966 --> 00:11:36,009
Your aunt...

228
00:11:38,428 --> 00:11:40,471
passed away about a-a year ago.

229
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,223
18 months.

230
00:11:43,433 --> 00:11:44,601
She used to help people.

231
00:11:45,143 --> 00:11:47,270
- She was a teacher, I think.
- Yes.

232
00:11:47,895 --> 00:11:48,980
Well, a counselor.

233
00:11:50,064 --> 00:11:52,734
We didn't tell him any of this,
swear to God.

234
00:11:53,109 --> 00:11:55,820
She really wants you to be happy
because she loves you...

235
00:11:56,988 --> 00:11:58,031
very much.

236
00:12:02,493 --> 00:12:03,536
That's it.

237
00:12:05,330 --> 00:12:07,999
I-I can't tell you how uncanny this is.

238
00:12:08,124 --> 00:12:09,167
I-I'm shivering.

239
00:12:11,002 --> 00:12:13,296
So, tell us about this case
you're working on with the FBI.

240
00:12:14,964 --> 00:12:17,383
"I'm not a detective.
I don't do police work."

241
00:12:17,508 --> 00:12:20,053
I'm just trying to help my colleagues
understand this man.

242
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,096
"How would you describe him?"

243
00:12:22,722 --> 00:12:25,892
"Well, cautiously, I would say
that he's obviously angry"

244
00:12:26,184 --> 00:12:27,977
probably in a lot of pain

245
00:12:28,645 --> 00:12:32,440
but I think he's trying to get in touch
with someone from the other side.

246
00:12:33,483 --> 00:12:34,609
What makes you say that?

247
00:12:35,818 --> 00:12:36,861
Who isn't?

248
00:12:38,404 --> 00:12:41,616
We have a call from Anna Marie
in Pflugerville.

249
00:12:41,741 --> 00:12:43,159
"Anna Marie, what's your question?"

250
00:12:43,284 --> 00:12:44,327
- Hey.
- "Hi."

251
00:12:44,452 --> 00:12:45,495
What's up?

252
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:47,288
Uh, Abbott sent me.
You can get outta here.

253
00:12:47,413 --> 00:12:49,499
- I'll take Jane home when he's done.
- Oh, no, I'm okay.

254
00:12:49,624 --> 00:12:52,210
No, forget it. You're beat. Go home.

255
00:12:54,921 --> 00:12:55,963
All right.

256
00:12:56,130 --> 00:12:59,008
"14 months ago. It was shortly after my
mother died."

257
00:12:59,634 --> 00:13:03,429
"Well, I was at home alone,
and I went into the room where my..."

258
00:13:13,314 --> 00:13:15,900
We have another call here from...

259
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:19,946
Lazarus, welcome to the show.

260
00:13:20,405 --> 00:13:22,699
Lazarus. Interesting name.

261
00:13:23,574 --> 00:13:24,784
"He rose from the dead."

262
00:13:25,993 --> 00:13:27,036
So I hear.

263
00:13:28,037 --> 00:13:29,288
What's your question, Lazarus?

264
00:13:29,664 --> 00:13:31,958
"What else do you know
about the man the FBI is hunting?"

265
00:13:32,834 --> 00:13:34,919
Well, I can't tell you everything
I know.

266
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:38,005
- "Why not?"
- Well, it's an ongoing investigation.

267
00:13:38,131 --> 00:13:40,633
The case is still open.
Why are you interested?

268
00:13:40,883 --> 00:13:42,510
Do you have information on the man?

269
00:13:42,844 --> 00:13:45,304
- "You're the one who knows everything."
- I never said that.

270
00:13:45,513 --> 00:13:48,266
"No, but you claim to be
in contact with his spirit."

271
00:13:48,391 --> 00:13:50,601
- Boss, you hearing this?
- Yes, we are.

272
00:13:51,352 --> 00:13:52,854
Wylie, how long until you trace
the call?

273
00:13:52,979 --> 00:13:54,021
I'm gonna need another minute.

274
00:13:54,605 --> 00:13:56,524
Make sure Jane keeps him
talking, okay?

275
00:13:56,941 --> 00:13:58,735
"If you're not, why would the police
want your help?"

276
00:14:00,069 --> 00:14:03,281
I get the feeling that you know more
about this case than you're saying.

277
00:14:03,823 --> 00:14:05,950
If that's so, you should probably share.

278
00:14:06,701 --> 00:14:07,744
"Why?"

279
00:14:07,952 --> 00:14:09,120
So we can catch him.

280
00:14:09,871 --> 00:14:11,122
"What if I don't want him caught?"

281
00:14:11,914 --> 00:14:13,166
Oh, why would you feel that way?

282
00:14:13,583 --> 00:14:15,668
"I spoke to someone like you
once before."

283
00:14:16,753 --> 00:14:17,795
Really? Who?

284
00:14:18,379 --> 00:14:19,964
"He was a complete fake."

285
00:14:20,131 --> 00:14:21,758
"You could practically see it
written on him."

286
00:14:24,010 --> 00:14:25,887
We didn't release
what was written on Gabriel's body.

287
00:14:26,012 --> 00:14:27,680
Nobody knows that except us
and the killer.

288
00:14:28,306 --> 00:14:29,348
That's our guy.

289
00:14:29,849 --> 00:14:32,059
That's our guy.
Uh, what's that address?

290
00:14:32,268 --> 00:14:33,936
- Hmm, interesting.
- What?

291
00:14:34,061 --> 00:14:35,146
He's not calling from a cellphone.

292
00:14:35,271 --> 00:14:36,898
He's calling from a landline...
normal phone.

293
00:14:37,398 --> 00:14:38,733
- Okay, that's the address, right?
- Yeah.

294
00:14:39,108 --> 00:14:40,777
Call downstairs. We need backup.

295
00:14:43,112 --> 00:14:45,281
When we left, you suggested
that you dealt

296
00:14:45,406 --> 00:14:48,284
with another psychic
who wasn't on the up-and-up.

297
00:14:48,409 --> 00:14:49,786
Are you a skeptic now?

298
00:14:50,119 --> 00:14:53,498
"No, I believe in spirits very much"

299
00:14:53,748 --> 00:14:55,666
"just not everybody who claims
to be in touch with them."

300
00:14:55,792 --> 00:14:57,168
Any spirits in particular?

301
00:14:57,752 --> 00:14:59,295
"You tell me. Who haunts you?"

302
00:15:00,129 --> 00:15:01,547
Me? Uh, nobody.

303
00:15:06,636 --> 00:15:08,054
"There must be spirits in your life."

304
00:15:08,471 --> 00:15:10,389
Well, fortunately,
they leave me alone.

305
00:15:33,579 --> 00:15:36,666
You still haven't told me whose spirit
you're trying to connect with.

306
00:15:36,791 --> 00:15:39,168
- "Have to go now. Bye."
- Hold on.

307
00:15:40,211 --> 00:15:41,254
Lazarus?

308
00:15:42,630 --> 00:15:43,673
Hello?

309
00:15:44,966 --> 00:15:46,759
Seems the caller has gone.

310
00:15:47,093 --> 00:15:49,220
We're gonna take a minute
for a station ID.

311
00:15:49,345 --> 00:15:52,557
We'll be right back
with Night Talk on KPQC.

312
00:15:56,435 --> 00:15:58,187
Abbott, what's happening?

313
00:15:58,354 --> 00:16:00,356
Something's wrong. He's not here.

314
00:16:00,690 --> 00:16:02,900
He rigged the phone.
We don't know where he is.

315
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:05,778
"I don't know what he's doing,
but I don't like it."

316
00:16:06,028 --> 00:16:07,989
You and Tork get out of there
and head back to the office.

317
00:16:08,114 --> 00:16:09,323
- "We'll meet you there."
- Okay.

318
00:16:12,034 --> 00:16:13,870
- Cho called. He said...
- Yeah, I heard. Let's go.

319
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:16,414
Hey, we're doing a show.
Hey!

320
00:16:18,541 --> 00:16:20,459
What happened to you?
I was listening. You got caught off.

321
00:16:20,877 --> 00:16:23,045
Yeah, the call was a ruse.
He's planning something.

322
00:16:23,170 --> 00:16:25,756
"You need to get back
to the office as soon as you can."

323
00:16:29,302 --> 00:16:31,178
Did you leave the door
of the Airstream open this morning?

324
00:16:31,387 --> 00:16:33,014
No. Maybe.
W-why?

325
00:16:35,182 --> 00:16:37,143
- It's open.
- "Okay, stop."

326
00:16:37,476 --> 00:16:38,644
Don't go anywhere near it.

327
00:16:38,769 --> 00:16:40,730
Don't do anything
until someone else gets there.

328
00:16:41,022 --> 00:16:42,648
That could take forever.
I'm gonna check it out.

329
00:16:43,524 --> 00:16:45,318
Yeah, fine, but you're not hanging up.

330
00:16:45,443 --> 00:16:46,903
Jane. We have to go.

331
00:16:47,194 --> 00:16:48,237
Just...

332
00:17:02,209 --> 00:17:03,252
Jane.

333
00:17:04,837 --> 00:17:05,880
Teresa, what's going on?

334
00:17:08,925 --> 00:17:11,427
There's nobody in here.
I guess we left it open.

335
00:17:12,386 --> 00:17:14,847
- Okay, get back to the office.
- All right, I'll see you there.

336
00:17:15,848 --> 00:17:16,891
Let's go.

337
00:17:34,305 --> 00:17:35,348
"Thank you for coming in."

338
00:17:35,849 --> 00:17:39,811
An hour and a half ago
two agents were attacked by a man

339
00:17:39,936 --> 00:17:43,273
who we believe is responsible
for 10 murders in the past year.

340
00:17:44,482 --> 00:17:45,525
This man.

341
00:17:46,192 --> 00:17:48,528
Agent Richard Tork is in the hospital.

342
00:17:48,695 --> 00:17:50,280
I've been told that he's gonna be all right.

343
00:17:50,738 --> 00:17:53,533
Patrick Jane, however,
has been abducted by this man

344
00:17:53,658 --> 00:17:55,118
and is still being held.

345
00:17:55,702 --> 00:17:58,997
So as of right now, no one goes home.

346
00:18:00,123 --> 00:18:02,834
No one takes a nap or a coffee break

347
00:18:02,959 --> 00:18:06,337
until Patrick Jane is returned
and this man is arrested.

348
00:18:07,839 --> 00:18:09,382
Agent Cho will have your assignments.

349
00:18:13,136 --> 00:18:15,388
We found the truck parked
a few blocks away.

350
00:18:15,555 --> 00:18:17,390
We assume the suspect
switched vehicles.

351
00:18:17,515 --> 00:18:20,852
All right, we need a team to sweep
security and traffic cameras in the area.

352
00:18:21,019 --> 00:18:22,103
Elias, that's yours.

353
00:18:22,562 --> 00:18:25,607
We also need fingerprint and DNA
evidence from the truck. Merrick.

354
00:18:25,732 --> 00:18:29,736
You warned me.
I didn't listen, and I am sorry.

355
00:18:32,238 --> 00:18:34,157
He could've killed Jane,
but he took him

356
00:18:34,991 --> 00:18:36,576
so that means he wants something

357
00:18:37,243 --> 00:18:40,788
and there is no one better at exploiting
a situation like that than Jane.

358
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:43,583
I hope you're right.

359
00:19:08,858 --> 00:19:09,901
Water?

360
00:19:12,904 --> 00:19:14,864
- No, thanks.
- Suit yourself.

361
00:19:19,285 --> 00:19:20,328
You know who I am?

362
00:19:22,622 --> 00:19:24,040
- Lazarus.
- That's right.

363
00:19:25,792 --> 00:19:27,001
You expect me to call you that?

364
00:19:27,669 --> 00:19:28,711
Don't be funny.

365
00:19:28,836 --> 00:19:30,338
Well, you're the one that came up
with the name.

366
00:19:42,266 --> 00:19:43,309
Interesting place.

367
00:19:44,477 --> 00:19:45,687
Could do with a little update.

368
00:19:46,688 --> 00:19:48,398
I saw you on TV.

369
00:19:51,859 --> 00:19:53,277
You said you know things...

370
00:19:55,321 --> 00:19:56,614
hear things.

371
00:20:00,618 --> 00:20:01,661
Prove it.

372
00:20:03,454 --> 00:20:04,831
It doesn't work like that.

373
00:20:05,456 --> 00:20:06,499
You did it on TV.

374
00:20:07,417 --> 00:20:08,793
Different circumstances.

375
00:20:10,044 --> 00:20:11,254
You can't just...

376
00:20:12,171 --> 00:20:13,589
you can't just make it happen.

377
00:20:14,924 --> 00:20:16,551
The other one said something like that.

378
00:20:16,676 --> 00:20:18,428
- You know who I mean?
- Sure.

379
00:20:19,303 --> 00:20:21,055
So, I tested him.

380
00:20:21,597 --> 00:20:24,851
He was a liar. Are you a liar?

381
00:20:25,309 --> 00:20:26,352
No.

382
00:20:39,073 --> 00:20:40,116
Prove it.

383
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:52,712
- Hi.
- Tork, please, go home.

384
00:20:53,087 --> 00:20:54,714
- I'm okay.
- This isn't your fault.

385
00:20:55,089 --> 00:20:56,924
Any of us had been there,
same thing would've happened.

386
00:20:57,216 --> 00:20:59,886
Yeah, but... I was there.

387
00:21:02,221 --> 00:21:03,264
I'll be at my desk.

388
00:21:08,644 --> 00:21:10,354
- I might have something.
- What?

389
00:21:10,688 --> 00:21:12,482
Jane said the killer was probably
doing something weird

390
00:21:12,607 --> 00:21:13,691
with the blood he took, right?

391
00:21:13,816 --> 00:21:16,861
So, I've been looking into local black
magic and occult connections.

392
00:21:16,986 --> 00:21:18,112
- Find anything?
- Too much.

393
00:21:18,237 --> 00:21:20,198
It's hard to find someone
who doesn't sound like a serial killer.

394
00:21:20,323 --> 00:21:23,534
But one place keeps cropping up...
a bookstore called The Grimoire.

395
00:21:23,659 --> 00:21:26,245
- The Grim, what?
- Grimoire. It's a magical textbook.

396
00:21:26,370 --> 00:21:28,539
Yeah, a lot of people interested
in the stuff go there.

397
00:21:28,956 --> 00:21:31,084
Maybe the killer did, too.
It seemed worth checking it.

398
00:21:32,376 --> 00:21:34,087
It's only three miles
from where the bodies were buried.

399
00:21:34,212 --> 00:21:36,714
Wylie, most of Austin is three miles
from where the bodies were buried.

400
00:21:36,839 --> 00:21:38,841
We appreciate the effort,
but it sounds thin

401
00:21:38,966 --> 00:21:40,343
and we don't have the time to waste.

402
00:21:45,681 --> 00:21:46,724
Jane would go.

403
00:21:47,809 --> 00:21:49,852
He'd say, "Do the usual thing,
you get the usual result."

404
00:21:51,062 --> 00:21:52,772
Which, in this case, is him dead.

405
00:21:54,982 --> 00:21:56,692
Okay, Wylie. Let's go check it out.

406
00:22:05,201 --> 00:22:07,120
This is your father's house, not yours.

407
00:22:08,371 --> 00:22:09,539
A spirit tell you that?

408
00:22:10,164 --> 00:22:11,207
No, the furniture.

409
00:22:13,459 --> 00:22:15,253
Your mother died
when you were very young.

410
00:22:15,837 --> 00:22:17,505
You were raised by your father.

411
00:22:19,549 --> 00:22:20,591
He was strict...

412
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:24,679
But you feel now that you deserved it.

413
00:22:25,638 --> 00:22:28,850
- He was right to punish you.
- Who's telling you that?

414
00:22:30,143 --> 00:22:31,602
It's what I'm getting from you.

415
00:22:32,979 --> 00:22:34,021
What else?

416
00:22:36,774 --> 00:22:38,776
You didn't have any friends
when you were a kid.

417
00:22:40,611 --> 00:22:41,821
You usually ate alone

418
00:22:42,363 --> 00:22:44,031
not because people
wouldn't sit with you

419
00:22:44,157 --> 00:22:48,369
but because you were disgusted
by the sounds they made when they ate.

420
00:22:50,371 --> 00:22:52,915
Sometimes, other people
don't feel real to you.

421
00:22:54,417 --> 00:22:57,211
They're like robots
wearing human skin.

422
00:22:58,546 --> 00:22:59,672
What do I do for a living?

423
00:23:01,257 --> 00:23:02,508
You're an exterminator.

424
00:23:04,969 --> 00:23:06,470
Yet, again, it doesn't feel real.

425
00:23:08,514 --> 00:23:10,850
It's like a movie being projected
on a screen.

426
00:23:13,019 --> 00:23:14,478
That's impressive.

427
00:23:15,479 --> 00:23:16,522
Thank you.

428
00:23:16,981 --> 00:23:19,150
But I don't need to know about me.

429
00:23:19,859 --> 00:23:21,527
I want contact with another.

430
00:23:23,905 --> 00:23:25,489
I don't sense any spirits here.

431
00:23:26,532 --> 00:23:29,452
You're wrong. The spirit is here.

432
00:23:29,577 --> 00:23:31,329
If you don't know that,
then you're a fraud.

433
00:23:31,454 --> 00:23:33,039
- No, I'm not.
- Just the like the other one.

434
00:23:33,164 --> 00:23:36,250
- I'm not a fraud.
- You're a liar and a cheat.

435
00:23:36,959 --> 00:23:38,002
You take it easy.

436
00:23:52,516 --> 00:23:53,559
Hello?

437
00:23:55,645 --> 00:23:57,104
No, ma'am. The job's finished.

438
00:23:58,731 --> 00:24:00,608
No. No, it's...

439
00:24:01,442 --> 00:24:02,485
Okay.

440
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:04,153
I'll address that. I'll be right over.

441
00:24:08,824 --> 00:24:09,867
I'll be back.

442
00:24:10,576 --> 00:24:11,953
- Hey.
- What?

443
00:24:13,329 --> 00:24:15,539
Uh, I could...
I could use that water.

444
00:24:21,462 --> 00:24:22,505
Thank you.

445
00:25:47,465 --> 00:25:49,967
- Kelis Weir?
- Kee-lis, yes?

446
00:25:50,134 --> 00:25:51,177
We're with the FBI.

447
00:25:51,927 --> 00:25:55,765
Forget it. I'm not collaborating
with religious persecutors.

448
00:25:56,307 --> 00:25:58,559
- What persecutors?
- We just wanna ask some questions.

449
00:25:58,726 --> 00:26:01,354
You say that, then you start in
with your western morality.

450
00:26:01,604 --> 00:26:02,938
Not fooling me twice.

451
00:26:03,439 --> 00:26:04,482
What do you mean?

452
00:26:04,732 --> 00:26:06,734
A while back, some guy
comes in, starts...

453
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:08,819
asking about Santeria.

454
00:26:09,195 --> 00:26:11,447
I tell him some friends
are performing a ritual.

455
00:26:11,572 --> 00:26:12,823
Oh, he shows up...

456
00:26:13,449 --> 00:26:17,453
with 10 cops, arrests everybody
for animal abuse.

457
00:26:17,578 --> 00:26:20,623
- Animal abuse?
- People cut up a million chickens a day.

458
00:26:20,790 --> 00:26:24,001
They put testicle-sized chunks
in a fryer, call it commerce.

459
00:26:24,126 --> 00:26:25,169
My friends...

460
00:26:26,253 --> 00:26:29,382
use one for an ancient
and sacred ritual

461
00:26:29,715 --> 00:26:30,758
and I go to jail?

462
00:26:31,425 --> 00:26:34,678
Hey, you're just all a bunch
of Judeo-Christian jackbooted thugs

463
00:26:34,804 --> 00:26:37,139
- as far as I'm concerned.
- Wylie, this is a waste of time.

464
00:26:37,264 --> 00:26:39,642
Hold on, hold on, hold on.
Kelis has a point.

465
00:26:39,767 --> 00:26:41,685
- She was duped. That isn't fair.
- Yeah.

466
00:26:43,104 --> 00:26:45,064
- So?
- So, maybe we can help you.

467
00:26:46,065 --> 00:26:47,108
How?

468
00:26:47,233 --> 00:26:49,151
If you talk to us, just answer
some questions

469
00:26:49,276 --> 00:26:51,946
we'll lean on Austin PD to reduce
your charges, maybe drop 'em.

470
00:26:52,071 --> 00:26:53,114
Why would they do that?

471
00:26:53,447 --> 00:26:54,949
The serial-killer case we're working on

472
00:26:55,241 --> 00:26:58,244
the mayor, Austin PD...
they want him in custody fast.

473
00:26:58,369 --> 00:27:00,538
If you help us make the arrest,
they'll owe us

474
00:27:00,663 --> 00:27:01,872
and we can use that to help you.

475
00:27:04,542 --> 00:27:05,584
He's right.

476
00:27:08,129 --> 00:27:09,171
What do you wanna know?

477
00:27:09,380 --> 00:27:11,507
We're looking for someone
who uses blood.

478
00:27:11,632 --> 00:27:13,259
A lotta people do that.
What kinda blood?

479
00:27:13,384 --> 00:27:14,427
Human blood.

480
00:27:15,344 --> 00:27:16,512
Okay, that's different.

481
00:27:17,138 --> 00:27:19,098
Those people do not come in here.

482
00:27:19,223 --> 00:27:20,724
I'm a little too vanilla for them.

483
00:27:20,850 --> 00:27:22,726
- Where do they go?
- The web mostly.

484
00:27:22,852 --> 00:27:25,688
There's a site called Blackmore.
Hardcores, they go there.

485
00:27:25,813 --> 00:27:27,148
I've been looking.
I haven't found that one.

486
00:27:27,273 --> 00:27:29,024
That's because you gotta go
deep web.

487
00:27:29,150 --> 00:27:31,235
You can't even find the site
without the IP.

488
00:27:32,862 --> 00:27:33,904
Can you give that to us?

489
00:27:35,990 --> 00:27:38,284
You're really gonna talk to Austin PD?
You're really gonna help me?

490
00:27:38,534 --> 00:27:39,577
Yes.

491
00:27:42,496 --> 00:27:43,539
Give me a minute.

492
00:27:48,711 --> 00:27:49,753
It's not bad, huh?

493
00:29:00,488 --> 00:29:02,323
The Blackmore site is huge.

494
00:29:02,348 --> 00:29:04,600
It's the eBay of the deeply weird.

495
00:29:04,725 --> 00:29:08,229
There are sections
on vampirism, self-vivisection...

496
00:29:08,354 --> 00:29:09,605
- Self-vivisection?
- Yeah.

497
00:29:09,730 --> 00:29:11,190
- Cutting yourself open.
- Okay.

498
00:29:11,315 --> 00:29:13,192
How does this help us find Jane?

499
00:29:13,568 --> 00:29:16,404
Well... there's also a section
on blood sorcery...

500
00:29:16,571 --> 00:29:18,239
Magical things you can do with blood.

501
00:29:18,364 --> 00:29:20,658
Now, you're supposed to use
your own blood, but...

502
00:29:20,783 --> 00:29:24,412
15 months ago, there was a discussion
on harvesting blood from other people.

503
00:29:24,537 --> 00:29:25,872
About 20 people were involved.

504
00:29:25,997 --> 00:29:27,498
Why would you harvest blood?

505
00:29:27,748 --> 00:29:28,875
Because you needed a lot.

506
00:29:29,041 --> 00:29:31,085
15 months ago...
that was right around the time

507
00:29:31,210 --> 00:29:32,712
our guy made his first kill.

508
00:29:32,837 --> 00:29:34,964
He could be one of those people.
Can we get their names?

509
00:29:35,089 --> 00:29:37,300
Well the screen names they used
are all super protected.

510
00:29:37,425 --> 00:29:40,970
However, I was able to dig one out...
A guy named Alan Saltonstall.

511
00:29:41,095 --> 00:29:42,555
A college professor in San Marcos.

512
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,806
- Let's go pick him up.
- Sure.

513
00:29:45,683 --> 00:29:47,768
- What do they do with the blood?
- A couple of things

514
00:29:47,894 --> 00:29:51,689
but the one that gets the most discussion
is a ritual that binds a spirit.

515
00:29:52,523 --> 00:29:54,275
- Bind. How?
- If you have a corpse

516
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,027
you can bind the spirit of a dead person

517
00:29:56,194 --> 00:29:57,528
by giving blood to their body.

518
00:29:57,778 --> 00:29:58,863
That way, the spirit never leaves.

519
00:31:00,132 --> 00:31:02,593
- Where are we with the search warrant?
- It's on its way to the judge right now.

520
00:31:04,178 --> 00:31:05,513
- Is that Saltonstall?
- Yeah.

521
00:31:05,638 --> 00:31:06,973
Well, why isn't somebody
talking to him?

522
00:31:07,098 --> 00:31:09,267
He requested an attorney.
He's on his way now.

523
00:31:09,392 --> 00:31:11,060
This guy could be torturing
Jane right now.

524
00:31:11,185 --> 00:31:13,062
- We don't have time for this.
- I'm sorry, Lisbon.

525
00:31:13,187 --> 00:31:15,106
- Let me talk to him.
- Look, the guy's lawyering up.

526
00:31:15,982 --> 00:31:17,024
Let me talk to him.

527
00:31:20,278 --> 00:31:21,320
Okay.

528
00:31:29,120 --> 00:31:32,164
I already told him I won't say anything
without my lawyer present.

529
00:31:32,665 --> 00:31:33,708
I don't care.

530
00:31:38,379 --> 00:31:39,422
You're hiding something.

531
00:31:40,673 --> 00:31:41,716
What?

532
00:31:41,841 --> 00:31:43,551
I never would've noticed something
like this before

533
00:31:43,676 --> 00:31:45,636
but I've been working
for a very long time

534
00:31:45,845 --> 00:31:48,139
with somebody who's good
at seeing into people

535
00:31:48,639 --> 00:31:50,308
what they're thinking, feeling.

536
00:31:51,642 --> 00:31:53,352
I can tell there's something
you're worried

537
00:31:53,477 --> 00:31:55,021
we're gonna find out about you.

538
00:31:55,354 --> 00:31:56,647
That's ridiculous!

539
00:31:56,772 --> 00:31:58,983
I'm guessing it has something
to do with the black magic

540
00:31:59,817 --> 00:32:02,486
something violent or sexual,
maybe both.

541
00:32:05,031 --> 00:32:06,699
But judging by how freaked out
you are

542
00:32:06,824 --> 00:32:08,576
I'd say it's something really bad.

543
00:32:08,701 --> 00:32:10,494
I am not freaked out.

544
00:32:10,620 --> 00:32:13,164
And my interests such as
they are, are purely academic.

545
00:32:13,289 --> 00:32:14,915
- I don't know what you think you're doing
- Shut up.

546
00:32:17,251 --> 00:32:19,962
"I don't care what kinda
kinky stuff you're in to."

547
00:32:20,087 --> 00:32:23,174
I have a friend who's in danger
and maybe you can help save him.

548
00:32:23,382 --> 00:32:25,384
It's possible he's being held
by somebody

549
00:32:25,509 --> 00:32:27,094
from that blood group of yours.

550
00:32:27,261 --> 00:32:28,387
I want their names.

551
00:32:28,512 --> 00:32:31,599
I don't know any names.
It's an online community, and...

552
00:32:32,058 --> 00:32:33,392
I shouldn't even be talking to you.

553
00:32:33,684 --> 00:32:36,562
You're lying. I can tell.
You have names.

554
00:32:36,771 --> 00:32:38,022
You've met them, some of them.

555
00:32:41,609 --> 00:32:44,528
I don't think you understand
how important this is to me.

556
00:32:44,987 --> 00:32:47,365
You give me a name, you can walk
out that door right now.

557
00:32:47,490 --> 00:32:50,868
You don't, and I will dig up
every dirty secret you have!

558
00:32:51,327 --> 00:32:53,621
- You'll what?
- I will tell everybody you know...

559
00:32:53,746 --> 00:32:55,623
your co-workers, your friends,
your family.

560
00:32:55,748 --> 00:32:57,291
You are not gonna be able to hide!

561
00:32:58,417 --> 00:32:59,710
Y-you're threatening me?

562
00:33:00,336 --> 00:33:02,046
It's not a threat.
It's a promise.

563
00:33:02,213 --> 00:33:05,341
You-you can't! That's...
that's illegal.

564
00:33:06,050 --> 00:33:08,636
My boss is right back there.
Tell him.

565
00:33:09,095 --> 00:33:11,889
Get me fired. Ruin my career.
I don't care.

566
00:33:13,115 --> 00:33:14,617
I want those names.

567
00:33:25,419 --> 00:33:27,463
He gave me eight names.
He says he can't remember the rest.

568
00:33:27,588 --> 00:33:30,341
- Good work.
- How do we know he's not the killer?

569
00:33:30,549 --> 00:33:31,592
We checked
his credit-card statements.

570
00:33:31,717 --> 00:33:33,177
He was outta the country
for two of the murders.

571
00:33:33,302 --> 00:33:35,596
Okay, we'll go out in pairs,
and I'll text you the names.

572
00:33:35,721 --> 00:33:37,723
Track 'em down. See if they're connected
to the killings.

573
00:33:37,848 --> 00:33:39,975
If you find a live one
let the rest of the team know fast.

574
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:06,377
Joe.

575
00:34:08,629 --> 00:34:10,256
He's here, your father.

576
00:34:11,382 --> 00:34:12,424
Big Joe.

577
00:34:13,384 --> 00:34:15,511
That's who you wanna get
in touch with, right?

578
00:34:17,304 --> 00:34:22,142
He says thank you for keeping him
for taking care of him.

579
00:34:25,354 --> 00:34:27,815
The passing over was hard,
but now he's good.

580
00:34:28,482 --> 00:34:30,025
His back doesn't hurt anymore.

581
00:34:30,651 --> 00:34:32,403
He feels better now than he ever did

582
00:34:32,528 --> 00:34:34,780
when Dr. Hannigan was feeding him
his meds.

583
00:34:41,412 --> 00:34:43,372
- There's doubt in you.
- No.

584
00:34:44,039 --> 00:34:45,916
- I-I mean...
- Put it aside. If...

585
00:34:46,500 --> 00:34:49,044
if you doubt, then I lose
the connection with him.

586
00:34:49,169 --> 00:34:50,671
I won't be able to communicate
with him.

587
00:34:51,046 --> 00:34:52,089
Okay.

588
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:57,553
He says there's a lake...

589
00:34:59,138 --> 00:35:02,182
- A lake Rickasee?
- Pickasee.

590
00:35:04,018 --> 00:35:05,060
Pickasee.

591
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:09,064
He didn't catch a fish that day.
No.

592
00:35:10,149 --> 00:35:13,485
No, you...
you caught a fish, a small one.

593
00:35:16,780 --> 00:35:17,823
Daddy.

594
00:35:18,657 --> 00:35:21,660
He wants to know
why you're keeping him here.

595
00:35:24,955 --> 00:35:26,498
There's something in me...

596
00:35:28,334 --> 00:35:29,376
a voice.

597
00:35:31,045 --> 00:35:33,464
And when it starts, I can't ignore it.

598
00:35:34,214 --> 00:35:37,885
I can't think about anything else
until I go out...

599
00:35:40,012 --> 00:35:41,096
find someone...

600
00:35:44,099 --> 00:35:45,351
And then it goes away again.

601
00:35:47,102 --> 00:35:48,145
For a while.

602
00:35:51,357 --> 00:35:52,900
Is that your voice, Daddy?

603
00:35:54,985 --> 00:35:59,406
Is that you in me?
Are you sending me out?

604
00:36:02,076 --> 00:36:03,243
Am I doing this for you?

605
00:36:06,872 --> 00:36:09,166
- He's saying something.
- What?

606
00:36:10,084 --> 00:36:11,126
Like...

607
00:36:14,505 --> 00:36:15,631
It's not clear.

608
00:36:16,340 --> 00:36:18,258
- It's not.
- No?

609
00:36:19,093 --> 00:36:21,345
Yeah, I'm so...
I'm-I'm sorry. I...

610
00:36:21,929 --> 00:36:22,972
He's...

611
00:36:23,430 --> 00:36:24,473
He's gone.

612
00:36:25,683 --> 00:36:26,725
Get him back.

613
00:36:28,435 --> 00:36:30,270
I can't. I need...
I need...

614
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:33,232
- An hour.
- Get him back.

615
00:36:33,524 --> 00:36:36,902
I need an hour. I just, I need to...
I need to rest.

616
00:36:37,194 --> 00:36:38,529
This is how this works.

617
00:36:42,199 --> 00:36:44,451
Hey, can I have some
of that gum, please?

618
00:36:49,331 --> 00:36:50,374
Thank you.

619
00:37:41,414 --> 00:37:43,667
We're looking for a man
named Joseph Keller Junior.

620
00:37:43,792 --> 00:37:45,627
According to our records,
his last known address

621
00:37:45,752 --> 00:37:48,213
was in an apartment building
that you manage, Ms. Martinez.

622
00:37:48,463 --> 00:37:51,716
- But then he moved out.
- Yeah, Keller, weird guy.

623
00:37:52,968 --> 00:37:55,095
Yeah, I think he moved
like two years ago.

624
00:37:55,303 --> 00:37:57,013
- Did he leave a forwarding address?
- No.

625
00:37:57,347 --> 00:37:59,516
I think he said something
about his dad being sick.

626
00:37:59,641 --> 00:38:02,435
Can you remember anything else
about him, where he worked?

627
00:38:02,727 --> 00:38:04,187
Some exterminator company.

628
00:38:04,604 --> 00:38:06,064
Do you know the name
of the company or the address?

629
00:38:06,648 --> 00:38:08,900
Maybe...
I think he sent me an e-mail about it

630
00:38:09,234 --> 00:38:10,277
wanted me to hire him.

631
00:38:11,528 --> 00:38:12,570
You want me to look for it?

632
00:38:12,696 --> 00:38:14,572
- That would be wonderful, thank you.
- Okay.

633
00:38:15,949 --> 00:38:16,992
I know it's in here.

634
00:38:22,330 --> 00:38:24,499
While you're looking for that
we're just gonna step outside.

635
00:38:24,666 --> 00:38:25,709
Okay.

636
00:38:27,961 --> 00:38:29,671
- Any news?
- Not yet, sorry.

637
00:38:29,796 --> 00:38:31,631
But I did find out something weird
about Keller.

638
00:38:31,798 --> 00:38:32,841
What?

639
00:38:32,966 --> 00:38:35,302
Not Keller Junior, but his father,
Joseph Keller Senior.

640
00:38:35,635 --> 00:38:38,221
15 years ago, there was a string
of killings in the area.

641
00:38:38,346 --> 00:38:40,181
Local PD took a hard look
at Keller Senior.

642
00:38:40,307 --> 00:38:42,767
Really liked him for them
but they only had a circumstantial case

643
00:38:42,892 --> 00:38:44,769
never found any conclusive
physical evidence.

644
00:38:44,894 --> 00:38:46,396
Keller's father was a serial killer.

645
00:38:46,855 --> 00:38:48,273
- Sounds like it.
- What happened to him?

646
00:38:48,398 --> 00:38:49,566
I don't know. Case went cold.

647
00:38:49,691 --> 00:38:51,234
Two or three years ago, he falls off
the map.

648
00:38:51,401 --> 00:38:53,778
He had a house not too far outta town,
near Lake Pickasee.

649
00:38:53,945 --> 00:38:54,988
You check out the house.

650
00:38:55,113 --> 00:38:56,614
I'll wait until she finds a work address
and head over there.

651
00:38:56,740 --> 00:38:57,782
Good.

652
00:39:06,833 --> 00:39:07,876
It's been an hour.

653
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:11,004
- He's here.
- He, what?

654
00:39:11,629 --> 00:39:13,298
He came back when you were gone.

655
00:39:13,631 --> 00:39:16,426
He wants to talk to you.
He's in there.

656
00:39:18,762 --> 00:39:20,722
- He wants to talk to me?
- That's right.

657
00:39:21,514 --> 00:39:23,600
If you want answers,
they're in that room.

658
00:39:24,684 --> 00:39:27,771
You can go in or not.
It's up to you.

659
00:39:36,363 --> 00:39:37,405
Do you smell gas?

660
00:39:39,324 --> 00:39:40,367
No.

661
00:40:48,101 --> 00:40:49,144
"Jane?"

662
00:40:49,561 --> 00:40:51,521
"Jane, are you in here?"

663
00:40:56,151 --> 00:40:57,193
Jane?

664
00:40:58,403 --> 00:41:00,196
Are you here?
Jane?

665
00:41:04,617 --> 00:41:06,411
Jane. Hey.

666
00:41:08,746 --> 00:41:10,582
Can you stand up?
Come on. Let's get you up.

667
00:41:11,791 --> 00:41:12,834
Oh, I got you.

668
00:41:16,546 --> 00:41:17,589
Come on.

669
00:41:26,264 --> 00:41:28,641
Don't you ever do that
to me again, ever.

670
00:41:48,495 --> 00:41:49,537
And sign here...

671
00:41:49,996 --> 00:41:51,372
and here...

672
00:41:53,166 --> 00:41:54,751
- And here...
- There.

673
00:41:55,418 --> 00:41:58,546
- And here. Yeah. That's it.
- Okay.

674
00:42:00,173 --> 00:42:01,216
It's all yours.

675
00:42:01,591 --> 00:42:03,593
Now, usually this is where
I hand over the keys

676
00:42:03,718 --> 00:42:05,053
but there aren't any.

677
00:42:06,679 --> 00:42:07,805
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

678
00:42:08,556 --> 00:42:10,642
- Thank you so much.
- You're very welcome.

679
00:42:12,560 --> 00:42:13,853
- Bye.
- Bye-bye.
